628 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 266 0 R
/E (In traditional retail and restaurant operations, the absence of an efficient Point of Sale \(POS\) system often leads to disorganized workflows, manual data management, and errors in inventory and transaction records. Many small businesses rely on manual methods or outdated software that lack the functionality required to meet the demands of modern operations. Manual systems require employees to input sales data and inventory updates, which can result in errors, inefficiency, and significant time consumption. These systems typically do not provide real-time inventory tracking or reporting features, making it challenging for business owners to monitor stock levels, analyze sales trends, or manage pricing effectively. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
629 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 266 0 R
/E (Additionally, manual or outdated systems fail to provide integration with modern technologies such as barcode scanners, QR code readers, or touch-screen interfaces, which are essential for faster and error-free transactions. The lack of a centralized system to manage sales, inventory, and customer details also results in lost opportunities for improving customer satisfaction and business efficiency. Consequently, there is a growing need for a POS system that not only automates routine tasks but also provides robust inventory management, sales tracking, and real-time data analysis to support business growth and decision-making. )
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
